      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hospitalization usually disrupts a person's privacy, autonomy, life style, roles, and finances. This article discusses the anxieties a patient can experience related to future uncertainties, insufficient information, fear of personal incompetence, being exposed to hospital rumors, and anticipated pain. Interventions to reduce patient anxiety are suggested."},
